        "created_at": "2026-05-15T16:24:57.410Z",
        "cooked": "<p><strong>Conclusion</strong><br>\nOver the course of ninety years of history, Venture Comics created dozens of popular characters, and hundreds more than never made much of an impression. From early heroes who faded away to villains who never made their mark, from new approaches that had to be undone to storylines that everyone quietly agreed to forget, the deep cuts of the line continue to fascinate long-time readers.</p>\n<p>Perhaps one day, some of the characters invented in these pages will be revived by a new writer, someone with a bold new vision and an approach that will let them pop off the page. Perhaps they will just be used as quick one-offs, when a battle scene is needed and you just don’t have time to develop a compelling villain.</p>\n<p>Perhaps your RPG table will be the place for these characters to shine, or to become a beloved meme or joke. All of them are failures, in their own way, but all of them were made with love. Someone hoped that they could make a difference, and if even one person grows to love them back, they’ll be a success.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Behind the Scenes</strong></em></p>\n<p>And by that I mean, this project has been a success because all of you are here.</p>\n<p>It’s not ending or anything, but Monday will mark the release of <em>Deep Cuts</em> and the conclusion of this thread. I’ll spend the week assembling the second thread, finding all of the links to where various parts of the project started and putting together a top page for the next period, and then on next Friday we will begin our environments.</p>\n<p>Thanks, folks. The support for this weird, increasingly-not-little project has been immense and gratifying. I’m glad folks are liking this odd creative project as much as I am.</p>",
